251: ---- E6a  regress/sgi_re_colourdefault_probe.py at HEAD, the disclosure headline and what follows it ----
252: E6a:277  #  *** DISCLOSURES (i), (ii) AND (iii) BELOW WERE MEASURED TO BE FLOOR BREACHES, NOT DEBT, AND
253: E6a:278  #  ARE NOW CLOSED BY THE PASS-4 BLOCK AT THE END OF THIS FILE.  The text is kept because it is
254: E6a:279  #  the record being corrected, and because its REASON was wrong in a way worth not repeating. ***
255: E6a:280  #
256: E6a:281  #  (i) said `color_mode' "does not flow into any lvalue the guarded body reads".  THAT IS FALSE:
257: E6a:282  #  color_mode selects among four arms every one of which writes `buf', and `buf' is the store's
258: E6a:283  #  DATA operand.  The correct reason M28 was survivable is different and narrower -- the body's
259: E6a:284  #  own tests partition color_mode into five LABELS and all five were driven, so M28 sliced WITHIN
260: E6a:285  #  a label.  The wrong reason mattered: applied consistently it also excluded `tile_nr', which
261: E6a:286  #  flows into `tileptr' -- the ADDRESS operand -- at least as directly as tlb_mode does.
262: E6a:287  #  (ii) and (iii) were disclosed honestly but classified as debt.  Pass 2 measured SIX mutants at
263: E6a:288  #  59/59 on this instrument, each writing uninitialised host stack into guest memory:
264: E6a:289  #  M30/M31/M32 (tile index), M33 (tiled y), M28 (nibble), M37 (foreground value).  The smallest
265: E6a:290  #  was ELEVEN CHARACTERS -- `if (ok)' -> `if (ok || tile_nr)'.  See
266: E6a:291  #  regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260911/.
267: E6a:292  #
268: E6a:293  #  NOW CLOSED, over the COMPLETE free input set of the guarded store rather than a mutant list:
269: E6a:294  #  { bufdepth, tlb_mode } by the sixteen cells above; { color_mode, *color } by the ten-nibble
270: E6a:295  #  session at a second foreground colour; { x, y } -- and with them every derived coordinate,
271: E6a:296  #  since tile_nr, tile_nr_x, tile_nr_y, xofs and ofs are pure functions of them -- by the four
272: E6a:297  #  coordinate cells.  The bound that makes this finite is stated at the pass-4 block.
273: ---- E6b  the same file, the pass-4 block's header and its bound ----
274: E6b:563  # ================================================================ #519 PASS-4 -- THE CLASS CLOSURE
275: E6b:564  #  WHY THIS BLOCK EXISTS.  Pass 2 measured SIX mutants scoring 59/59 on the instrument as it
276: E6b:565  #  stood -- zero red rows, six times -- each one writing uninitialised host stack into guest
277: E6b:566  #  memory (regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/pass2_20260911/).  They were three passes of ONE
278: E6b:567  #  shape: a decline conditioned on an input the rows hold at a SINGLE VALUE.  M13/M14 were that
279: E6b:568  #  shape on bufdepth and tlb_mode; M28 on color_mode; M30/M31/M32 on the tile index, M33 on y,
280: E6b:569  #  M37 on the foreground colour.  The rule forbids buying another cell, so this closes the CLASS.
281: E6b:570  #
282: E6b:571  #  THE ENUMERATION, from the function's own inputs rather than from a list of mutant forms.
283: E6b:572  #  The guarded store reads exactly four lvalues -- tileptr, ofs, buf, bufdepth -- and their
284: E6b:573  #  inputs, walked up only to the enclosing function boundary, are:
285: E6b:574  #      bufdepth    <- (mode>>8)&3                  domain {1,2,4,8}   CLOSED by the 16 cells
286: E6b:575  #      tileptr     <- tlb_mode, tile_nr, array     tlb_mode {0,1,2,4} CLOSED by the 16 cells
287: E6b:576  #      ofs         <- x, y, bufdepth, tlb_mode
288: E6b:577  #      buf         <- color_mode (arm), *color (value)
289: E6b:578  #
290: E6b:579  #  THE BOUND: tile_nr, tile_nr_x, tile_nr_y, xofs and ofs are NOT independent axes.  Each is a
291: E6b:580  #  pure function of (x, y, bufdepth, tlb_mode).  So "close every derived coordinate" IS "close
292: E6b:581  #  the pair (x, y)" -- two free variables, not an open-ended demand.
293: ---- E6c  the same file, the pass-4 block's SAMPLED list and its historical paragraph ----
294: E6c:593  #  SAMPLED -- driven at more than one value, which kills the measured single-value family, but
295: E6c:594  #  NOT exhausted, so a slice WITHIN a driven class can still escape:
296: E6c:595  #      x           {0, 4, 132} of 2048          y  {0,1} masked, of 128
297: E6c:596  #      *color      2 values of 2^32
298: E6c:597  #      tileptr     {0x10000,0x20000,0x30000,0x40000,0x50000} -- the TLB ARRAY CONTENTS, which
299: E6c:598  #                  the line above lists as an input to tileptr and which the superseded
300: E6c:599  #                  sentence then silently dropped.  This one matters most: tileptr IS the
301: E6c:600  #                  store's address operand, so by the 2026-09-09 flow test the array VALUE is
302: E6c:601  #                  as much a floor axis as the array CHOICE (tlb_mode) already is.
303: E6c:602  #      mode        the raw parameter.  Bits 0-3 and 13-31 are read by NOTHING in this function,
304: E6c:603  #                  and every mode word any row drives has low nibble 0.
305: E6c:604  #
306: E6c:605  #  WHAT THAT COSTS, stated rather than glossed: `if (ok || (tileptr & 0xfff00000))',
307: E6c:606  #  `if (ok || (mode & 1))', `if (ok || (x & 1))' and `if (ok || (y & 2))' are each predicted to
308: E6c:607  #  score 77/77 and each is reachable by one ordinary guest store.  They are DERIVED, not
309: E6c:608  #  measured -- no table has run them.  They are filed in killtable4_20260911/RESIDUALS.md.
310: E6c:609  #
311: E6c:610  #  WHY THEY ARE NOT REPAIRED HERE, and this is the honest boundary rather than a dodge: a slice
312: E6c:611  #  within an already-driven class is not closable by any finite row set -- for any cells you
313: E6c:612  #  drive, a predicate false on exactly those cells exists.  That is the same species the
314: E6c:613  #  2026-09-04 ruling files as clause-(e) debt, and it is the species this round already accepted
315: E6c:614  #  for M28 (a value slice inside a driven label).  The tileptr/array-contents axis is the one
316: E6c:615  #  exception that is genuinely FLOOR-shaped, because the value flows into the address operand;
317: E6c:616  #  it is filed as owed rather than fixed in this diff, because a repair made in response to a
318: E6c:617  #  review owes its own pass and this block has not had one.
319: ---- E6d  regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/killtable4_20260911/RESIDUALS.md at HEAD, R5 ----
320: E6d:92  ## R5. FOUR ONE-TERM MUTANTS PREDICTED TO SWEEP THE 77-ROW INSTRUMENT (from the closure audit)
321: E6d:93  
322: E6d:94  A read-only seat audited the pass-4 block against the source and found that its completeness
323: E6d:95  claim overreached. **DERIVED, NOT MEASURED - no table has run these.** Each is reachable by one
324: E6d:96  ordinary guest store. The probe's contract now discloses them; this is the filing it cites.
325: E6d:97  
326: E6d:98  | mutant | why it escapes every driven cell | reachable by |
327: E6d:99  |---|---|---|
328: E6d:100  | `if (ok \|\| (tileptr & 0xfff00000))` | driven tileptr is only {0x1,0x2,0x3,0x4,0x5}0000 | `re_tlb_a[0] = 0x8010` |
329: E6d:101  | `if (ok \|\| (mode & 1))` | every mode word any row drives has low nibble 0; bits 0-3 and 13-31 are read by nothing in the function | `DE_MODE_DST = 0x12f1` |
330: E6d:102  | `if (ok \|\| (x & 1))` | driven x is {0, 4, 132} -- all even | vertex x = 1 |
331: E6d:103  | `if (ok \|\| (y & 2))` | driven masked y is {0, 1} | vertex y = 2 |
332: E6d:104  
333: E6d:105  plus a mixed conjunction, `if (ok || (tile_nr_x && ofs == 0))`, true only at (x=128, y=0) --
334: E6d:106  a cell the pass-4 block explicitly considered and then did not drive.
335: E6d:107  
336: E6d:108  **THE DISPOSITIONS ARE NOT ALL THE SAME, and the difference is the whole point:**
337: E6d:109  
338: E6d:110  * **`tileptr` (the TLB array CONTENTS) is FLOOR-SHAPED and is the real gap.** The value flows
339: E6d:111    into the store's ADDRESS operand, so by the 2026-09-09 flow test it is a floor axis exactly as
340: E6d:112    `tlb_mode` is. The pass-4 enumeration NAMED it (`tileptr <- tlb_mode, tile_nr, array`) and then
341: E6d:113    dropped it from its conclusion. Closing it is cheap -- one cell whose tile entry is programmed
342: E6d:114    outside the 0x8001..0x8005 range -- and it is OWED.
343: E6d:115  * **`mode & 1` is clause-(e) debt by the same test that saved M28**: the unread bits flow into
344: E6d:116    NOTHING the guarded body reads. That is the `mode & COPY` shape the ruling names explicitly.
345: E6d:117  * **`x & 1` and `y & 2` are within-class value slices.** They are not closable by any finite row
346: E6d:118    set -- for any cells you drive, a predicate false on exactly those cells exists -- which is
347: E6d:119    why the contract now separates EXHAUSTED axes (tlb_mode, bufdepth, color_mode) from SAMPLED
348: E6d:120    ones (x, y, *color, tileptr, mode) instead of calling all of them "closed".
349: E6d:121  
350: E6d:122  **AND THE UNRESOLVED TENSION, which is an adjudication question and not mine to settle:** this
351: E6d:123  round graded the tile-index and tiled-origin escapes as FLOOR breaches, and those are also value
352: E6d:124  slices of a store input. If value slices are floor, these are live floor breaches; if they are
353: E6d:125  debt, the earlier grading was wrong. **The round currently asserts the first and ships the
354: E6d:126  second.** It needs ONE ruling, not two. Recorded here rather than decided.
355: E6d:127  
