40: E1:89  **So the measuring seat's FLOOR grade of the tile-index family was wrong AS A GRADE, and the codex class-closure review of 2026-09-11 was right** (*"BECAUSE THE BODY NEVER TESTS `tile_nr` FOR ZERO, `M30` ... IS NOT A FLOOR AXIS UNDER THE BODY-TESTED-PARTITION RULE -- IT IS CLAUSE-(e) DEBT"*).  The data-flow sentence the seat used (*"flows into the address operand at least as directly as `tlb_mode` does"*) is the 2026-09-09 LABEL clause with its first half dropped: a dispatch LABEL becomes a floor axis when its value flows into a body-read lvalue -- `tlb_mode` is a label the body tests as a case AND flows into `tileptr`; `tile_nr` flows and is not tested as a case.  Flow alone is the transitive-chasing reading the 08-24 bound forbids.
41: E1:90  
42: E1:91  **Harder on the author's leaning, as the brief asks.**  The author leaned YES (floor, L2, a repair owing its own pass).  YES would have reopened a chain the receipt closed ("NO FURTHER PASS IS OWED") on a mutant that no instrument in the tree can see; it would grade by consequence, which D1 refused; and its warrant is the rejected finiteness bound.  And harder on NO, because NO carries a real cost: `ok || (tileptr & 0xfff00000)` keeps the instrument green while re-opening the uninitialised-`buf` store on every real framebuffer tile at a physical address `>= 1 MB` -- the `M30` shape (fix kept on the instrument, open on the world).  The carrier's answer to that is the one it gave at `#549`: severity ORDERS the debt and does not promote it.  So the row is filed at the TOP of this file's coverage debt, below its live defects (`sgirebufuninit`, med), and it costs ONE readback.
