46: E1:95  **EXHAUSTED / SAMPLED: ADOPTED as clause-(e) disclosure vocabulary, with one correction.**  It is exactly what clause (e) asks for -- *"write into the CONTRACT which cells are covered and which are deliberately not"* -- made explicit per axis.  Definitions: EXHAUSTED := every cell of the BODY-TESTED partition of that lvalue is rowed (floor discharged on that axis); SAMPLED := driven at two or more values, with the untested slices and their derived or measured sweeps named.  The probe's `:587` wording "every value in the reachable domain is driven" coincides with the partition definition for `tlb_mode`/`bufdepth`/`color_mode` (tiny domains) and must not be the definition: the next probe with a 2^32 operand could never write EXHAUSTED under it and would write it anyway for a 16-value field the body tests at one bound.  BOUND: a disclosure vocabulary can never DEMAND a row (the carrier's filter rule: *"a filter can reject or repair a row; it can never demand a new one"*), so it cannot grow.  STRUCTURAL LANDING SPOT, per the structure-first rule: the PRETABLE block's GUARD FIELD vs BODY FIELD check gains one column, "partition the BODY induces on this lvalue" (the codex 09-11 table is the exemplar), and EXHAUSTED/SAMPLED is read off that column rather than asserted.  A template line, not a checker.
