    #519 (sgirandomcolour): the colour-mode PUT default arm stored four host random() bytes into guest memory -- reachable with the documented DE_MODE_TYPE_YCRCB -- and now declines the store with a latched announce
    
    `horrible_getputpixel()`'s PUT switch fell through unsupported colour types
    (12 of 16 encodings, YCRCB among them) to a default arm that filled `buf`
    with `random()` and stored it: a destination pre-painted 0x11223344 read
    0x56e8857a and 0x38abc4e1 on two runs.  Now the arm clears `ok`, the store
    is guarded by `if (ok)`, the destination keeps what the guest had, and the
    announce is latched once on its own SGIRE_W_BADCOLOR bit.
    
    WITNESS, rung 3 (agy, the independent-transport fallback): committed 2/5,
    fix 5/5, same script (regress/artifacts/sgirandomcolour/witness_20260910/,
    fix_20260910/).
    
    DETECTOR: regress/sgi_re_colourdefault_probe.py, 89 assertions, now wired
    into gate_arm.sh (new section after sgirandompixel; parse-before-score, the
    denominator pinned to a literal 89).  gate 14 PASS (914 checks), the new
    section green; log killtable5_20260912/gate_arm_89rows.log.
    
    *** THE CLASS CLOSURE, AND EVERY LEG OF ITS TABLE LANDED ON PREDICTION. ***
    The probe's controlling CONTRACT declares the projection
    {TLB_A, TLB_B, TLB_C, LIN_A} x {bufdepth 1,2,4,8} x {latch clear, set on
    entry}: 32 cells, 21 occupied before, 11 empty.  Codex's closure design
    (codex_closurediff_20260912b.txt) filled the eleven, widened the four
    existing depth-8 readbacks to both words, and added an M28-family row.
    Kill table 5 (killtable5_20260912/SCORES.txt; PRETABLE written first):
    
        BASE           89/89        NIB_OTHER_ZERO  78/89 (ten nibble rows + M28 nib60)
        HEAD           28/89        TAIL8_ZERO      81/89 (all eight depth-8 rows)
        ten FIRST_* controls and REPEAT_L1_ZERO: 88/89 each, on its OWN row
    
    The closing pass (codex_passE_20260912.txt) verified the enumeration WITH its
    denominator: 0 of 32 cells unoccupied; 11 isolated-cell kills measured, 21
    predicted from source and fixture.  Disclosed, not closed: bare `ok =
    (<pred>)` mutants with an uninitialised buf (identical-byte writes are
    invisible), and the exact historical M28/M28r edit.
    
    TWO WRONG RECORDS OF MINE, corrected in PRETABLE.out's appended section:
    GUARD/BODY called the latch a dominating predicate of the store (it governs
    the diagnostic only -- it is a chosen mutation axis); CLAIM->ROW credited the
    whole projection to the additions (they cover 16 of 32 cells).  AND A THIRD,
    found by the codex CHANGELOG drafting pass: PRETABLE claimed "mtime proves
    order" and my post-table append then REWROTE its mtime.  The surviving order
    evidence (pre-append mtime 02:26:35 CDT observed before launch; SCORES header
    02:27:41 CDT) is recorded there; post-table notes now go in a separate file.
    
    The CHANGELOG block was drafted by codex from the recorded evidence (its
    draft and a per-number source list are kept at
    codex_changelogdraft_20260912.txt), then checked here against the artifacts
    before landing.  Two briefs of this round were refused by the codex
    cybersecurity filter and answered once re-worded as plain mutation testing.
    
    check_probe_wiring.py classifies the detector and its eleven untracked
    instruments.  Nothing pushed (LOCAL GIT ONLY).
    
